  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Classify Stationary Point Using Second Derivative</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Consider the function:</p>
\[ f(x) = {@f_expr@} \]
<p>The derivative is \(f'(x) = {@f_prime@}\), which satisfies \(f'({@x0@}) = 0\), so \(x = {@x0@}\) is a stationary point.</p>
<p>Classify the nature of the stationary point at \(x = {@x0@}\):</p>
<p>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Compute the second derivative of \(f(x)\):</p>
\[ f''(x) = {@f_double_prime@} \]
<p>Evaluating at \(x = {@x0@}\):</p>
\[ f''({@x0@}) = {@f2_at_x0@} \]
<p>Because \(f''({@x0@})\) is {@d2_reason@}, the stationary point is classified as a <strong>{@ans_label@}</strong>.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1000000</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber>demo-stationary-point-radio</idnumber>
    <stackversion>
      <text>2025102100</text>
    </stackversion>
    <questionvariables>
      <text><![CDATA[/* Stationary point classification */
x0: rand([-2, -1, 1, 2, 3]);
scenario: rand([1, 2, 3]);
c_const: rand([-5, -3, 1, 4, 7]);

f_expr: if scenario = 1 then expand((x - x0)^3/3 + (x - x0)^2 + c_const)
        else (if scenario = 2 then expand(-(x - x0)^3/3 - (x - x0)^2 + c_const)
        else expand((x - x0)^3/3 + c_const));

ans_label: if scenario = 1 then "Local minimum"
           else (if scenario = 2 then "Local maximum"
           else "Point of inflection");

d2_reason: if scenario = 1 then "positive (f''(x_0) > 0)"
           else (if scenario = 2 then "negative (f''(x_0) < 0)"
           else "zero (f''(x_0) = 0)");

correct_val: scenario;
wrong_val: if scenario = 1 then 2 else 1;

f_prime: diff(f_expr, x);
f_double_prime: diff(f_prime, x);
f2_at_x0: ev(f_double_prime, x = x0);

/* Model answer for radio input widget */
ta1: [
  [1, is(correct_val = 1), "Local minimum"],
  [2, is(correct_val = 2), "Local maximum"],
  [3, is(correct_val = 3), "Point of inflection (second derivative test inconclusive)"]
];
]]></text>
    </questionvariables>
    <specificfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[[[feedback:prt1]]]]></text>
    </specificfeedback>
    <questionnote format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[{@scenario@}, {@x0@}, {@f_expr@}]]></text>
    </questionnote>
